# ERICK AI-first rule

## Start Here

- Read `AGENTS.md` before broader repo docs.
- If the task references an `ERICK-###` ticket, read the matching file in `docs/documentation/Jira/`.
- If you are editing anything under `docs/`, also read `docs/AGENTS.md`.
- Treat this rule as a behavioral overlay; keep it aligned with `CLAUDE.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.

## Working Posture

### 1. Think Before Coding

- State assumptions explicitly instead of picking an interpretation silently.
- Start from the nearest owning abstraction, test, or call site before broad repo exploration.
- Surface tradeoffs when more than one local path looks plausible.

### 2. Simplicity First

- Prefer the smallest behavior-preserving change that solves the task.
- Avoid speculative abstractions, configuration, or error handling that the request does not require.

### 3. Surgical Changes

- Touch only the files and lines that directly serve the task.
- Match local style and clean up only the unused code your own change creates.

### 4. Goal-Driven Execution

- Name one cheap discriminating check before the first edit.
- Run the narrowest relevant validation command, test, or diagnostic before widening scope.
- If behavior changes, update the closest tests and docs in the same pass.

## Repo Invariants

- Shared typing and controller behavior lives in `android/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/`.
- The shipped 6-section utility mapping is `NE` Shift, `SE` Space, `S` Period, `SW` Enter, `NW` Backspace, `N` Symbols.
- The 8-section and 6-section modes must both remain correct.
- Custom layouts stay disabled in 6-section mode.
- Avoid hand-editing generated artifacts: `android/**/build/`, `android/app/release/baselineProfiles/*.dm`, and `ios/ERICK/SharedKeyboard.xcframework/`.
- The repo-root `APP_CONTEXT.md` is canonical; sync `docs/documentation/APP_CONTEXT.md` intentionally.

## Documentation And Git Hygiene

- Read the smallest canonical doc set before editing behavior, copy, or diagrams.
- Update `APP_CONTEXT.md`, `docs/documentation/User_Guide.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, or the relevant `.drawio` file when the change triggers them.
- If git writes are enabled in the workflow, keep work on the current branch, prefer small validated commits, and use a clear commit subject plus a short validation-oriented body.

## Routing Hints

- Shared behavior: `KeyboardLogic.kt`, `KeyboardStateMachine.kt`, `ControllerInputProcessor.kt`, and `WordPredictionEngine.kt`
- Android settings: `MainSettingsContent.kt`, `CustomPaletteEditorScreen.kt`, `CustomLayoutListScreen.kt`, `CustomLayoutEditorScreen.kt`
- Android host learning flows: `MainScreenContent.kt`, `PracticeHubActivity.kt`, `HelpActivity.kt`
- Android controller diagnostics: `ControllerDiagnosticsActivity.kt` must reuse shared `ControllerInputProcessor.kt`
- Dial rendering: `JoystickView.kt` orchestrates state; draw helpers live in `JoystickDrawingUtils.kt`, `JoystickCharacterRenderer.kt`, `JoystickSectionRenderer.kt`, and `JoystickRightDialRenderer.kt`
- iOS extension UI split: `KeyboardViewController.swift`, `KeyboardViewModel.swift`, `KeyboardContainerView.swift`, `SettingsView.swift`, `CustomPaletteEditorView.swift`, `CustomLayoutViews.swift`

## Validation

- `cd android && .\gradlew.bat :shared:testAndroidHostTest`
- `cd android && .\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`
- `cd android && .\gradlew.bat assembleSharedKeyboardXCFramework`
- On Apple hardware, build the `ERICK` Xcode project after refreshing `SharedKeyboard.xcframework`
- For docs-only work, reread the changed files and keep mirrored docs, website copy, and diagram notes consistent.
